{
  "requirement": "`habeas status` and the mdBook requirements index MUST generate their Definition/Evidence Markdown tables through the same renderer. That renderer MUST calculate column widths, align the columns, and display the same evidence-state labels in both outputs. Callers MAY select different definitions and supply different kind-labeled name cells so mdBook can link to detail pages.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict: the requirement is met.** Both outputs build their tables through one renderer, and the code and tests cover the stated obligations.\n\n**Shared renderer**\n- `render_evidence_table` in `src/markdown.rs` (marked `{impl}`) is the only table generator. It calculates the widest cell in each column, including the \"Definition\" and \"Evidence\" headers. It left-aligns and pads the header, the `---` separator row, and every data row to those widths.\n- `habeas status` calls it from `status_markdown_with_options` (`src/commands.rs`, marked `{impl}` at the function and at the call site).\n- The mdBook index calls it from `DetailPlan::populate` (`src/index.rs`, marked `{impl}` at the call site).\n\n**Same labels**\n- Both callers take the evidence-state text from `evidence.state().label()`, which is `EvidenceState::label` in `src/index.rs`. The labels therefore cannot differ between the two outputs.\n\n**Different selections and name cells**\n- Callers choose their own rows. `status` filters by glob, by `--all`, and by verbose and state, and uses plain `` `name` (kind) `` cells.\n- mdBook uses every detail-page definition and supplies cells linked to the detail pages, as ``[`name`](href) (kind)``.\n- The renderer takes `(String, &str)` rows, so it accepts any name cell.\n\n**Tests**\n- `index_shows_evidence_states_and_links_generated_chapters` (`src/index.rs`, marked `{test}`) checks the mdBook output. It covers the Valid, Determination false, Invalid, and Missing labels, the linked name cells, and identical `|` positions on every row.\n- `status_tables_align_each_column_to_its_widest_cell` (`tests/commands.rs`) covers the `status` side for both `status` and `status --all`. It checks pipe alignment, widths equal to the widest cell, and the `---` separator. It is marked for `status_table_alignment` rather than this requirement, but it exercises the same renderer.\n\n**Minor observations (not gaps)**\n- Widths use byte length (`.len()`), which could misalign non-ASCII names. Definition names are presumably ASCII, so I do not count this against the requirement.\n- No test calls both outputs on the same input to compare them directly. Using one function for both is what guarantees they match, so that seems acceptable.\n\nAll implementation sites are marked, and I found no unmarked behavior beyond what the requirement and other cited definitions specify.",
